## Code Writing Rules for CAMEL

### Import Patterns

#### Single Agent
```python
from camel.agents import ChatAgent
from camel.models import ModelFactory
from camel.types import ModelType

# Create model (platform is auto-inferred from ModelType)
model = ModelFactory.create(
    model_type=ModelType.GPT_4O_MINI,
)

# Create agent
agent = ChatAgent(system_message="You are helpful.", model=model)
response = agent.step("Hello")
```

#### Workforce (Multi-Agent)
```python
from camel.agents import ChatAgent
from camel.models import ModelFactory
from camel.societies.workforce import Workforce
from camel.tasks import Task
from camel.types import ModelType

# Create agents
model = ModelFactory.create(model_type=ModelType.GPT_4O_MINI)
researcher = ChatAgent(system_message="You are a researcher.", model=model)
writer = ChatAgent(system_message="You are a writer.", model=model)

# Create workforce and add workers
workforce = Workforce('Research Team')
workforce.add_single_agent_worker(
    'Researcher who finds information',
    worker=researcher,
).add_single_agent_worker(
    'Writer who writes reports',
    worker=writer,
)

# Process task
task = Task(content="Research and write about AI trends.", id="0")
workforce.process_task(task)
```



