Content: The DeepWiki MCP server at https://mcpservers.org/servers/devin/deepwiki is not responding within the default timeout period, causing a connection timeout error.

The script to create an MCPAgent with DeepWiki MCP tools and query the architecture of the camel-ai/oasis repository is as follows:

```python
import asyncio
from camel.agents import MCPAgent
from camel.models import ModelFactory
from camel.types import ModelType

async def main():
    # Define the DeepWiki MCP server configuration dictionary with correct type
    deepwiki_config_dict = {
        "mcpServers": {
            "deepwiki": {
                "type": "streamable_http",
                "url": "https://mcpservers.org/servers/devin/deepwiki"
            }
        }
    }

    # Create the model
    model = ModelFactory.create(model_type=ModelType.GPT_4O_MINI)

    # Create the MCPAgent with the DeepWiki config dict as local_config
    agent = MCPAgent(
        model=model,
        local_config=deepwiki_config_dict,
        function_calling_available=False,
    )

    # Use the agent asynchronously
    async with agent:
        query = "Retrieve the architecture of the camel-ai/oasis repository."
        response = await agent.astep(query)
        print("Response:")
        print(response.msgs[0].content)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    asyncio.run(main())
```

This script is saved at `task-script/single_agent/5_deepwiki_mcp_agent.py`.

Note: The connection to the DeepWiki MCP server timed out, which may be due to server unavailability or network issues. You may want to check the server status or increase the timeout in the MCPToolkit configuration if supported.

